## Troubleshooting

### 1. DLP Policy is Not Triggering or Blocking Content

This is the most common issue reported. If you have configured a DLP policy but it fails to inspect or block traffic, the cause is nearly always that the traffic is not being decrypted. DLP inspection requires an active **TLS Decryption** policy to scan the content of HTTPS requests.

**Incorrect Configuration (Will Not Work):** A policy that does not explicitly enable decryption.

| Selector      | Operator | Value          | Logic | Action  |
|---------------|----------|----------------|-------|---------|
| Domain        | in       | `box.com`      | AND   | Block   |
| DLP Profile   | in       | `Credit Cards` |       |         |

**Correct Configuration:** To fix this, create a Gateway HTTP policy that enables TLS Decryption for the traffic you intend to inspect. Ensure this decryption policy has a higher precedence (is ordered before) your DLP policy.

**Step 1: Create a Decryption Policy**

| Selector        | Operator | Value          | Logic | Action    |
|-----------------|----------|----------------|-------|-----------|
| Domain          | in       | `box.com`      |       | Decrypt   |

**Step 2: Create Your DLP Block Policy**

| Selector      | Operator | Value          | Logic | Action  |
|---------------|----------|----------------|-------|---------|
| Domain        | in       | `box.com`      | AND   | Block   |
| DLP Profile   | in       | `Credit Cards` |       |         |

<Aside type='note'>
For a detailed guide, refer to the documentation on [configuring TLS decryption](/cloudflare-one/policies/gateway/http-policies/tls-decryption/).
</Aside>

